NIGHT_LOADED({"seed":1084,"generated_at":"2026-10-21T06:00:00Z","chain":[1,3,4,2,5],"frame":{"collector":"J.D.","intro":["You are the new assistant.","On the table lies a note from the collector.","The key to the front door is in his coat, and he has gone home.","The clock says a quarter past nine.","You begin to sort."],"note_table":"File twelve envelopes.\nCabinet five stays shut.\nLock up before twelve.\n— J.D.","note_final":"Well filed. Tomorrow at nine. — J.D.","card_desk":{"kind":"Legend","description":"In the Central Legend Archive there is a reading table with a green cloth, and on it a lamp with a green shade. Along the wall stand five cabinets with drawers full of cards. In the evening, when the others have gone, the assistant who worked late sits there and reads. Only the hands can be seen in the lamplight.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":1936,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","teller":"the previous assistant","note":"Don’t read it. File it."},"trail_notes":["Not recorded by me. My previous assistant.","Same hand. He worked on into the evenings.","His last. No more cards from him after that.","This one he did not file. Nor did I."],"card_five":{"kind":"Legend","description":"There was once a new assistant at the Legend Archive who stayed on one evening to finish the filing. The collector had gone home. The assistant put four cabinets in order and then opened the fifth as well, though it was to stay shut. After that the assistant was never seen again. The cards lay neatly in order, and what the assistant saw there was ____.","place":"Amsterdam","prov":"N.-H.","year":"tomorrow","teller":"J.D.","initials":"J.D.","code":null},"final_words":["nothing","me","myself","the assistant","the previous assistant"],"door_locked":"Locked. The key is in J.D.’s coat.","midnight":"The clock strikes twelve.","good_end":"Well done. Cabinet five stays shut.","nee":"No.","not_yet":"Not yet.","into_envelope":"Into the envelope.","archive_note":"You need not go behind the divider tonight.","finish_first":"Not yet. Cabinet {roman} first.","digit_note":"{n}. The number of cabinet {roman}.","digit_first":"Remember: the lock of cabinet V wants four of these.","found_notes":{"chair":"One is where I put it down yesterday.","lamp":"One is under the lamp. Don’t move the lamp.","coat":"One is in my coat. Leave the coat hanging.","typewriter":"One is still in the machine."},"floor_note":"That one does not belong in that drawer.","machine_continued":"— continued in drawer 3 —","reactions":{"reopen_filed":"That one was done.","stalled":"Hurry up.","read_desk":"I said: don’t read it.","typo3":"It is there. Read.","other_hand":"he is not coming back","five_shut":"Shut."},"citation":"Source: Dutch Folktale Database (Nederlandse Volksverhalenbank), Meertens Institute (KNAW), www.verhalenbank.nl"},"cabinets":[{"id":1,"label":"Omens","digit":4,"drawers":[{"id":"1-1","type":"P2","difficulty":2.8016,"rank":0.0098,"note":"No place. Somewhere between the other three. Pin it on the map.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN006308","role":"target","render":{"description":"The chattering of a magpie is a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of danger, a marriage or a death.","place":null,"prov":"L.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208668","original":"Wanneer men in het bos een ekster hoort slaan, dreigt er gevaar. Het kan er ook op duiden, dat er binnenkort \"een bruiloft of een lijk\" komt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"LINSSEN002305","role":"helper","render":{"description":"Seeing three magpies is an omen of a death.","place":"Sint Odiliënberg","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208317","original":"Als iemand drie eksters bij elkaar zag, dan zou iemand uit de familie sterven.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[51.14333,6.0]},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN007410","role":"helper","render":{"description":"The chattering of a magpie is an omen of a death or an accident.","place":"Leveroy","prov":"L.","year":1964,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208799","original":"Het schateren van een ekster was een aanwijzing dat binnenkort iemand uit de familie zou sterven of dat hem een ongeluk zou overkomen.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[51.24917,5.84722]},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LINSSEN009208","role":"helper","render":{"description":"The number of magpies determines whether they are a voorloop (an apparition foreshadowing an event) of good or bad luck.","place":"Sint Joost","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208963","original":"Voortekens . Wanneer drie eksters zich toonden in de nabijheid van een huis, stond er groot geluk te verwachten. Een ekster daarentegen was een voorbode van ongeluk.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-1","geo":[51.1175,5.89861]}],"hints":["Three places are there already. The fourth lies between them.","Within 2 hours’ walk of Sint Joost.","Find Heel on the map."],"lock":{"kind":"place","target_geo":[51.17917,5.89444],"radius_km":6.0},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c1","field":"place","value":"Heel"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":null},{"id":"1-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.2279,"rank":0.4361,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1607","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Werewolves wore chains, so you could hear them coming from far away. People were upset then.","place":"Nieuwaal","prov":"Gld.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/125803","original":"Vroeger bij Sprokkelenburg onder Heukelum, daar woonde de machinist van 't stoomgemaal, die spookte daar ook. Van die verhalen dat d'r werwolve ware, diere met een ketting aan, dat je ze al van verre kon hore. De mense ware dan zo van streek.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"cab:3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ027402","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman once heard a lot of noise in an adjoining room. But there was nothing to see. The next day a relative fell through the floor and landed in that room. That was the sound the woman had heard the day before.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21587","original":"Ik wie op in kear by myn suster yn Twizelerheide. Wy sieten yn 't keammerke togearre by elkoar, doe hearde ik dat it der yn 'e oare keamer hiel bot oan wei gong. Myn suster fornaem it net. Ik sei: \"Hwat in lawaei.\" Wy der hinne. Mar der wie neat to sjen. Dat wy gongen wer nei 't keammerke ta to thédrinken.\nDe oare deis rekke de dochter fan myn suster troch de souder hinne boppe de keamer. De planken bijoegen har. Dat joech in stik leven. En dàt hie ik de foarige deis heard.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ026709","role":"member","render":{"description":"A woman often hears a voice in her dreams that makes predictions to her. She also often hears the sound of hammering in places where new houses will be built.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21442","original":"Yn 'e droom hear ik faek in stem. Dy dielt my dan it ien of oare mei. Dêrtroch wyt ik fan alles, hwat der gebeure sil.\nIk haw trije beppesizzers, dy moesten alle trije in pop ha. Dy stem sei tsjin my: Twa derfan dat wurde jonges. Se komme allebeide Anders to hiten. (Ik wist net dat de heiten fan 'e manlju beide Anders hieten)\nTsjin 'e trêdde beppesizzer sei 'k: \"Dû krigest in famke.\" Dat is ek útkaem. It woarde tsjin my sein. Dat binne fisioenen.\nSa't ik sei, ik hear hiel faek timmerjen, sawol by dei as by nacht. En 't komt altyd nei.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ026702","role":"member","render":{"description":"One winter afternoon a woman heard a car in the yard, but she saw nothing. There were no car tracks to be found in the snow either. But the next day there was an accident on the road, and lots of people and cars came into the yard.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0487","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21435","original":"It gebeurde in pear jier lyn. 't Wie yn 'e winter, der lei snie. 't Wie op 'e neimiddei. Ik hearde in protte lawaei op 'e wei en by ús op it hiem. Ik hearde ek in greate auto. Doe't ik op it hiem kom wie der alhiel neat to sjen. En doe't ik de oare moarns doe't it ljocht wie, nei spoaren socht yn 'e snie, wienen dy der net. Doe wist ik it oare wol. De oare deis is hjir doe in ûngelok gebeurd op 'e wei. 't Wienen allegear auto's en minsken, ek hjir op it hiem. Se ha hjir doe noch in frou yn 'e hûs brocht.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-2"}],"hints":["Look at the numbers in red pencil.","Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The card about Nieuwaal belongs with the Werewolves."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":3},"on_success":{"trail_note":0,"unlock_cabinet":3,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"1-3","type":"R1","difficulty":1.1281,"rank":0.3431,"note":"The clock has stopped. These three know the time.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"Voda_022_16","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A clergyman saw his own funeral. Four men with a bier kept walking behind him all night. He later died on that same road.","place":"Eindhoven","prov":"N.-Br.","year":1977,"code":"SINSAG 0481","initials":"H.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/129749","original":"Een geestelijke uit Oirschot zag eens zijn eigen begrafenis. Op een nacht ging hij van Oirschot naar Best. Daar hoorde hij achter zich iemand lopen. Toen ie omkeek, zag ie vier mannen die een baar droegen. Hij wilde wachten, maar toen hie stil bleef staan, bleven ook de dragers stilstaan. En als ie verder ging, gingen ook de dragers verder. Zo bleven deze vier mannen met de baar de gehele nacht achter de geestelijke lopen. Die was blij dat ie eindelijk in Best aankwam, waar hij van de schrik kon bekomen. Enige tijd later moest de geestelijke weer naar Best. Daar stierf hij plotseling. Toen droeg men het lijk van de geestelijke over dezelfde weg die hij gelopen had toen de dragers met de baar hem volgden.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ099406","role":"omen","render":{"description":"When a dog howls eerily, someone in the neighbourhood will die within 4 days.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0486","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36651","original":"As in houn spûkgûlde seinen se, gong der binnen fjouwer dagen ien dea yn net to fiere omtrek.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ065203","role":"omen","render":{"description":"A group of boys once called names at an old woman who was said to be a witch. The woman made as if to jump across the four-metre ditch, and the boys ran off as fast as they could. She often had to get up at night to see funeral processions.","place":"Twijzelerheide","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/27375","original":"Hjir wenne yn Twizelerheide in âld minske, dat wie Minne Ael, dy gong foar in tsjoenster troch. Hja wie nachts faek warber. Hja wenne oan 'e Swâdde. Dy wie sa'n fjouwer meter breed.\nOp in kear skelden in pear jonges har út, dy wienen oan 'e oare kant fan 'e Swâdde. Doe die se in pear stappen achterút en sei: \"Ik sil jim krije\", krekt as soe se in oanloop nimme.\nDoe naeiden dy jonges hurd út.\nHja moest der nachts út as der in lykstaesje ûnderweis wie.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"1-3"}],"hints":["Read them again. All three count something.","The same number three times. That is the time.","4 o’clock. Set the clock."],"lock":{"kind":"clock_hour","hour":4},"on_success":{"chime":4,"digit":{"value":4,"card":"c1"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3"]}}]},{"id":2,"label":"White Women","digit":6,"drawers":[{"id":"2-1","type":"P4","difficulty":1.9078,"rank":0.9943,"note":"Torn in two. The rest is in the box on the table.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"ZEEUW053","role":"top","render":{"description":"A farmer's son returning home from the fair at night is addressed at a haunted spot by a white lady, who asks him to release her and so make his fortune. He agrees, and each time the ghost orders him to do something he says: \"Do it yourself!\" as the ghost had","place":"Overslag","prov":"Zl.","year":1916,"code":"SINSAG 0301","initials":"L.M.d.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38979","half":"top"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"KOOIJMAN0043","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Beautiful, but also frightening. She rose straight up. It lasted only a few seconds, then she had vanished again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"DYKFRIES2187","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"These were malicious spirits and ghosts that carried people and children off to their lair. Later these beings were called witte juffers (white ladies), but these were friendly and helpful by nature.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ007910","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"People did not dare go there at night, because the white woman drove them to the side towards the little lake. Without doing anything themselves, they ended up in the lake.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"LYST030","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In return she must run naked through the church. She does so reluctantly. Later a wit wief (white woman) can be seen on the land she was given. People are convinced that the woman's ghost still haunts it.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0311"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"CJ005402","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"In the Zwagerbosch he suddenly saw five women standing there wearing pointed caps and long white skirts. There was not a breath of wind, yet the plumes of the caps waved to and fro. He was frightened to death and went to old Bearn's farm. When they went to look together, the women were gone.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"LYST007","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"When a mother who also has a fake baby in her cradle decides to take the child to the nuns so it can learn to talk, she meets a wit wief (white woman) on the way. The white woman asks the child whether it is going to be baptised. Suddenly the child can talk and tells the white woman it is going to the nuns. The mother then knows she is holding a fake child and drops it on the ground. A farmer who wants to see the tricks of the witte wieven up close hits one of them on the shoulder with a heavy stick. The witte wieven then decide to return to Germany. On their journey to Germany one of them can walk no further. The others bury her alive, with the promise that she will rise again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c8","story_id":"VODA_044_03","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"He wants to invite her to dance with him at the Whitsun feast. When he reaches the Berg, he sees a white figure: the lady. She beckons him to stop. She seizes Bart and drags him into a whirling round dance. In the end Bart is left as limp as a dishcloth. His horse has gone home, and his household come looking for him and bring him home. But Bart never recovers and dies within three days.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c9","story_id":"ZEEUW049","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"Since then Miss Jenne has not been seen again.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c10","story_id":"YPFOE070a","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"One evening, after a party, one of Durk Jaringa's sons passed that crossroads and saw a white figure floating just in front of him. He ran head over heels back to Jistrum. Later some others took him home past the crossroads, but there was no longer anything to be seen of the figure.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c11","story_id":"LAAN004a","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"On the border of Slochteren and Schildwolde they walked up and down an oak avenue in long white robes. They were never seen by day, but they were not afraid. They were in eerie places and in churchyards. They were also always at places where something had happened.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0310"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c12","story_id":"ZEEUW054","role":"distractor","render":{"description":"There were 3 chests, with a dog on one and on the 2nd a lion holding the key to the 3rd in its mouth, which the man has to take. He does not dare, and the woman takes leave for 100 years.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"},{"id":"c13","story_id":"ZEEUW053","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"told him to beforehand. The ghost leads him through passages, doors and halls until they come to 5 chests, on which sits a big black dog that takes his breath away. He can no longer speak, and the ghost takes leave for 100 years; the man is back on the road where he was addressed, drags himself home and is dead 2 days later. Someone heard of his adventure and also tried his luck, saw a light dancing ahead of him at midnight, took fright and fled.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0301"},"home":"2-1"}],"hints":["Read the top piece to the last word. What is mentioned already?","The top piece breaks off in mid-sentence. The bottom one finishes it.","The number is SINSAG 0301. There are three with that number in the box."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c13"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c13"],"stack":["c1","c13"]},"found_card":{"card":"c13"}},{"id":"2-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3535,"rank":1.0009,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"KEUNING011705","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"A white apparition stands still in the middle of a little bridge.","place":"Easternijtsjerk","prov":"Fr.","year":1963,"code":null,"initials":"S.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/131602","original":"Sa seach ien hjir ek ris sa 'n forskining midden op in planke, dy oer de sleat laei, stean. Mar dy bleau dêr stiif stean, dat de man is werom gien.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:5"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ020208","role":"member","render":{"description":"One evening people once saw two witte wijven (white women).","place":"Jistrum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/20586","original":"Freark en Wytske wennen op 'e Iest to Jistrum. Ik wenne yn dy tiid by de boer, 'k wie fyftsjin jier. Hja fortelden op in joun, se hienen to jounpraten west. Doe't se weromkommen en op 'e hoeke wienen, hienen dêr twa âlde wite wiven west.\nSy hienen deabinaud west en koenen foar noch achterút. In hiel skoft bleauwen se stean. Doe't se letter thús kommen wienen se noch sa forbouwerearre, dat sy koenen earst net in wurd útbringe.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ035001","role":"member","render":{"description":"At a haunted spot a white lady on a horse used to be seen often. She is a ghost woman.","place":"Harkema","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22709","original":"Op 'e Lytse Wei by de Harkema ried froeger in wite dame op in hynder, doe wie de Lytse Wei noch in sânpaed.\nDurk Pitstra hat har us njonken him hawn op in joun, doe siet er op syn eigen hynder om dat yn 't lân to bringen. Hwat hurder hy ried, hwat hurder dat frommes tasette. Hy koe har net kwyt wurde en dreau op 't lêst yn 't swit.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ045113","role":"member","render":{"description":"Witte wieven (white women) used to haunt a haunted spot.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24238","original":"Op dit ein fan 'e Folgerster loane spoeken froeger wite wiven.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"2-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about the devil.","The card about Easternijtsjerk belongs with the Devil."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c1","cabinet":5},"on_success":{"trail_note":3,"unlock_cabinet":5,"stack":["c2","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"2-3","type":"R2","difficulty":1.1679,"rank":1.0,"note":"Something is written on the window. Don’t wipe it off.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ015603","role":"card","render":{"description":"A fisherman sees a lady in white clothes and decides to follow her. But the wit wief (white woman) vanishes as quickly as she appeared.","place":"Broeksterwâld","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19893","original":"Douwe syn broer Anne Feddema hie to fiskjen west. Hy hie nei 't tichtset ta west en farde de Lyts út wei werom de kant nei de brêge út. Doe kom der in juffer oan yn sniewite klean. Hy tocht: Ik wol wite hwer't dy keart, dat hy hie 't eech net fan har ôf. Doe't er oan har ta wie, died er de fêstsetter yn 'e kant en krekt doe't er dat die, wie de wite juffer fuort.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"WEV010904","role":"card","render":{"description":"A maid living with two wicked men stabs one of the men to death and flees. The other man pursues her and, just as she shuts the stable door, throws an axe after her. The axe was fixed in the stable door of a new farmhouse as a reminder.","place":"Ter Borg","prov":"Gr.","year":1965,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/43395","original":"Mien mouder vertelde mie n verhoal dat in Roswinkel gebeurd is. \n\nWazzen n moal twai heksn, dai n kind stooln. \nZe brochden dat kind noar twai keerls tou. \nDoor wur ze meid, man zai kreeg dr ook n stuk of wat kinder bie. \nTwintig joar is ze dr wol west.  De keerls leefden van roof en stelerij. \n Op n dag was de aine keerl vot. De ander mos eevn scheerd worn. \nt Wicht grip t mes en snit de kerel de haals oet. En dou dr vandeur. Man intied komp de ander in hoes en zug wat er gebeurd is. Hai grip de haksebiele en neit achter t wicht aan.  \nIn Roswinkel hef hai heur inhoald. Hai smit de biele op heur, man t is net te loat; zai was net n boerderij inloopn en har de voldeure achter zuk tou trokn. Door kwam de biele in terechte. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"YPFOE070b","role":"card","render":{"description":"There was once a man who went with his dog cart from Hardegarijp to Bergum. A white figure travelled with him the whole way.","place":"Burgum","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0310","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12147","original":"Wite juffers\nDer wie ris in man, dy reizge mei de hûnekarre de Simmerdyk del fan Hurdegaryp nei Burgum. It wie jûn en tige mistich. Hy siet yn 'e hûnekarre en njonken him siet in wite gestalte. De hiele tiid is dy njonken him meireizge, oan Burgum ta. Dy man hat in benaud oerke trochmakke.","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"LYST075","role":"card","render":{"description":"At a wedding one of the guests remarks that they forgot to invite the witte wieven (white women). When someone mockingly calls out to the witte wieven, an axe is thrown at his head. He just manages to flee inside in time. The door still shows the marks of the axe. The witte wief (white woman) calls out that she could have caught him if she had not lost her little shoe.","place":"Zenderen","prov":"Ov.","year":1953,"code":"SINSAG 0161","initials":"M.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13289","original":"Parallel met het verhaal van de \"spinvisite\" loopt ook 't verhaal van de \"brulfte\" (bruiloft) waar een van de gasten tegen de \"brulfteneugers\" opmerkt dat hij de \"nögste noabers\" n.l. de \"witte wieve\" heeft vergeten. De \"brulfteneuger\" laat dat niet op zich zitten, gaat naar buiten en nodigt \"de witte wieve\" uit, op spottende toon. Hij wordt onmiddelijk achterna gezeten, vlucht nog net binnenshuis, terwijl hem de bijl nagegooid wordt en 'n snee in de niendeure maakt die nog aan de kleinkinderen van het bruidspaar vertoond wordt. Hier hoort ook weer dezelfde klacht over 't schoentje bij, dat niet was vastgestrikt.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"TINNEV065","role":"sill","render":{"description":"A man goes to cut grass stalks with six others when the first man suddenly starts screaming. The group starts running. When they have stopped running, the first man tells them he saw a grijze juffer (grey lady).","place":"Didam","prov":"Gld.","year":1944,"code":"SINSAG 0310F","initials":"A.T.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/22411","stain":"six"},"home":"2-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"YPFOE088","role":"card","render":{"description":"A farmer has two sons. One cannot be got out of bed in the morning, the other has to do all the work. At some point he is fed up with it and wants to wake his brother up properly. In doing so he hits him on the temple, and his brother dies. The family moves away because they can no longer cope. The linden tree has kept on blooming. The murdered boy still haunts the area.","place":"Goutum","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0311","initials":"Y.P.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/12173","original":"It spoek yn 'e Foksegatten\nDe wei fan Feanwâldsterwâl nei Hurdegaryp troch de Foksegatten wie foarhinne in sânreed. Op healwei stie yn in bocht in boerespul, dêr't in famylje de Vries op wenne. Twa fan 'e soannen slepten yn it bûthûsbedsteed. Ien fan 'e jonges wie moarns min fan 't bêd te krijen en dan strûpte de oare foar 't wurk op. Dêr krige dy syn nocht fan en op in moarntiid kaam er foar 't bêd mei in tuolle yn 'e hân. Hy woe him in tikje jaan om him wekker te krijen, mar hy rekke him by ûngelok oan 'e sliep, dat er it bestoar. Syn folk wie slim oerstjoer en ferslein, foaral de broer, dy't himsels ferwiet, dat er net better oppast hie.\nDe famylje koe der net langer bankje en fûn in oar hinnekommen. De pleats waard ôfbrutsen. …","lang":"Frisian","front":"description"},"home":"2-3"}],"hints":["Read it from back to front.","It begins with D.","Didam. Lay that card on the windowsill."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c5","object":"window","text":"Didam"},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":6,"card":"c5","word":"six","stained":"c5"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6"]}}]},{"id":3,"label":"Werewolves","digit":7,"drawers":[{"id":"3-1","type":"P5","difficulty":0.679,"rank":0.375,"note":"The tellers contradict each other. Go by the oldest.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LYST274","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a wolf at night disappears when the farmer finds a wolfskin under his bed and burns it.","place":"Drogteropslagen","prov":"Dr.","year":1937,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"K.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/13538","original":"Vroeger was hier een knecht, die 's nachts in een wolf veranderde en het de mensen dan lastig maakte. Onder zijn bed vond de boer op zekere dag een wolfshuid en verbrandde die. Sedert was de knecht verdwenen.\n(Verteld door een zeventig-jarige).","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"VVUNL301","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand becomes a werewolf by means of a leather belt, which he hides. It is found and burnt in the oven; at once the suspected farmhand comes rushing up on horseback, but he is held back, and when the belt has burnt he says: \"I am freed!\"","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1920,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"F.S.S.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35840","original":"De weerwolf \n\nOp de hoeve Bosscherhof woonde eertijds een knecht die een lederen riem bezat, welke de macht had, hem, indien hij hem omgordde, te betoveren als weerwolf. Geheimzinnig en zorgvuldig werd deze band telkenmale door de knecht verstopt en wat men ook deed, hoe men ook spiedde, men vond hem nooit. En geregeld hadden de mensen uit de omtrek, die laat huiswaarts keerden, de weerwolf te dragen. En ook iedereen herkende steeds de knecht. Men gaf elkander raad om wanneer men overvallen werd, de weerwolf op een of andere manier te prikken of te krab-ben tot hij bloed voelde of zag. Dan was men gered. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN002605","role":"variant","render":{"description":"A farmhand who turns into a black cat at midnight by means of a rim is released after the rim is burned.","place":"Baexem","prov":"L.","year":1962,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208342","original":"Volgens tweede verteller was er op Nelishof te Tungelroy een knecht die elke nacht tussen twaalf en een uur afwezig was. Door een raampje ging hij naar buiten. Hij klom dan op de schansenhoop en kwam er als kat af. De boer had hem bespied en gemerkt dat boven op de schansenhoop een velg lag van een karwiel. Die had de boer daar niet neergelegd en hij zocht verband tussen de spokerij (zwarte kat) en dat karwiel.\nDit zou hij vernietigen als de knecht afwezig was. Op zekere dag had hij hem met schapen naar Antwerpen gestuurd. Toen hij een dag weg was stak de boer zijn bakoven aan en wierp de velg erin.\nOp hetzelfde moment verscheen de knecht en wilde de oven in. Het gelukte slechts met drie man om hem daarvan te weerhouden. …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":null,"role":"summary","render":{"description":"In Limburg an animal was seen: ____. (according to the oldest recording)","place":null,"year":null,"code":null,"initials":"J.D.","summary":true},"home":"3-1"}],"hints":["Look at the years.","The oldest is from 1920.","That card names an animal. Which?"],"lock":{"kind":"word","salt":"92011994ce294905","accepted_hashes":["72bae2bbd2fd628b8012c1e4c68798038ff7795c8a269854f094eaf1d05daf03","7af91a2ed66092ba00170b737bfeefddc99184f4dc64eee2fe005860d2e2c708","cd0da0586bdf83c3b41af194464648270725c1c8a33f26b4404edc050e5a1eb6","e261cce7703e694cef558a95585a5de392130d890a7bd5cbfa8f162c68c888c4","e6afe176514c8863e177e0747fdbfc7afcd1160d442ed642abc3e999d3624efc"],"fill":"c4"},"on_success":{"fill_field":{"card":"c4","field":"blank","value":"typed"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"3-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.1235,"rank":0.5492,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"LINSSEN010706","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf jumps on someone's back, disappears after being wounded so that it bleeds.","place":"Susteren","prov":"L.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209104","original":"WEERWOLF. Deze viel 's avonds de mensen lastig op eenzame wegen. Hij sprong hen op de rug. Wanneer de drager evenwel een scherp voorwerp of een mes bij de hand had, en de weerwolf die de voorpoten om de nek van de drager had geslagen, bloedend kon verwonden, was van zijn last bevrijd. \nDe weerwolf nam dan de vlucht.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ014205","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"At the end of the Wâl a foal haunts the place with a porridge pot around its neck.","place":"Feanwâldsterwâl","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/19631","original":"Op 'e ein fan 'e Wâl oan 'e Hurdegariper kant spûke altyd in fôlle mei in brijpot om 'e hals.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:4"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"LINSSEN009004","role":"member","render":{"description":"Werewolf makes itself carried as far as a crossroads.","place":"Echt","prov":"L.","year":1965,"code":null,"initials":"G.H.L.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208948","original":"Weerwolf: Pustjens van Dieteren had een oom die Toon heette. Het was een stroper, die de weerwolf had gedragen van de \"Boombrug\" tot waar deze weg kruiste met een andere weg. Bij een kruising van wegen liet de weerwolf altijd los.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"EGGEN005301","role":"member","render":{"description":"Fake werewolf who makes himself carried is struck down.","place":"Aalbeek","prov":"L.","year":1971,"code":null,"initials":"C.E.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/208115","original":"tijd : rond 1900\nplaats : aalbeek en omgeving.\n\nonderwerp: \"weerwolf\".\n\n[1.] \nin aolbik houwe ze völ te doon mèt de weerwóuf. es eine door 'ne sjtegel mòs, kaom 'r 'm 'nt dràge.\nmèh dat waor geinen echten weerwouf, dat waor eine, wat dat veur de gekkerie deeg. de wèts wie dat geit: vèl um, get kweke, en ederein zwoa bang make, tot ze neet dorsjte houwe.\ntot eine gèt dapperder waor es dae grapjas. dae houw 'ne flìnke sjtek bie zich, en dao heef 'm neer. daomèt kante ze 'm, want den anderen daag laog 'r dao.","lang":"Limburgish","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"3-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a ghost.","The card about Feanwâldsterwâl belongs with the Ghosts."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c2","cabinet":4},"on_success":{"trail_note":1,"unlock_cabinet":4,"stack":["c1","c3","c4"]}},{"id":"3-3","type":"R3","difficulty":1.0236,"rank":0.3077,"note":"When someone knocks: count. That card under the door.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ044011","role":"door","render":{"description":"One of seven sons is a werewolf. You must never quarrel with a werewolf, because then he will kill you. A girl always did sewing at other people's homes. Her suitor once asked her for a handkerchief. She gave it to him, and outside he tore the thing to shreds. After that he was normal again. He turned out to be a werewolf. Then the girl broke it off.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1968,"code":"SINSAG 0823","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/24049","original":"Ien fan sawn soannen wie in wjerwolf. As in wjerwolf jin kriget, makket er jin dea, seinen se froeger tsjin ús. Men mat der noait rûzje mei krije, sei in muoike yn 'e Westerein, dan pakke se jo.\nMyn wiif hat in kammeraetske hawn, dy naeide altyd by oare minsken. Dy hie forkearing mei in feint.\nOp in kear wie er by har, doe frege er har om har bûsdoek. Hja hie him de bûsdoek jown, mar doe hied er dy bûsdoek yn alle moster forskuord bûtendoar.\nLetter wie er wer goed west, mar 't is wol útrekke tusken dy beiden. Hwant hy wie in wjerwolf.\nHja hat it sels oan myn wiif forteld. Dat kammeraetske wenne oan it Wyldpaed.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"HOL001024","role":"card","render":{"description":"People who do not touch werewolves; a man who is out as a werewolf is in two places at once; werewolves wear a skin.","place":"Opheusden","prov":"Gld.","year":1962,"code":null,"initials":"A.R.H.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/209732","original":"Gaart en Stoffel van Brenk konden weerwolven. Als deze en ook andere personen daarmee bezig waren, moest men ze niet “omlegge” op het bed, want dan ging het mis met hen. Mensen zagen \"Stomp\" onder de noteboom liggen, maar ook lag hij thuis op bed. Hij was toen aan het weerwolven. Weerwolven hadden een vel om.","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"VVUNL049","role":"card","render":{"description":"Every evening after dinner Sjang goes out and does not come back until very late. One time they follow him and see him take something out of a tree, and a moment later he was a werewolf. The priest is fetched and Sjang has to produce his things. Out came a sheepskin and a red stick with a red ribbon; these are burnt in the oven while three men hold Sjang down. When everything is charred, he says he is freed.","place":"Kessel","prov":"L.","year":1952,"code":"SINSAG 0824","initials":"J.N.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/35588","original":"De geplaagde herder \n\n't Gebeurde op 'Gravenhof' te Kessel, tussen 1860 en '70. Sjang van de Maas uit Neer was hier scheper; een onnozele, rustige kerel, die niemand kwaad deed, en elke dag zijn schapen hoedde. Maar na een tijdje maakten de boer en de boerin zich over hem ongerust. Elke avond na het eten verdween Sjang plotseling en keerde pas heel laat in de nacht weer huiswaarts. Dit werd zo verdacht dat men op een keer de knaap stilletjes achtervolgde... Men zag toen dat hij tot de holle boom liep, even voorbij het Annakapelletje; daar nam hij iets uit. Na enkele ogenblikken veranderde hij van gedaante, en stoof als schrikaanjagende weerwolf met een geweldige vaart weg. . . …","lang":"Standard Dutch","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KOOIJMAN1182","role":"card","render":{"description":"There used to be a woman in Blokland who claimed that every evening between half past ten and twelve she heard the werewolf raging outside.","place":"Blokland","prov":"Utr.","year":1963,"code":"SINSAG 0804","initials":"H.K.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/72678","original":"De weerwolf, de weerwolf. Nou je 't zegt. D'r woonde vroeger in Blokland een vrouw. Die woonde daar op d'r eige alleen. En die vrouw die beweerde, ze hoorde iedere avond de weerwolf buite tekeergaan. Iedere avond tusse half elf en twaalf uur. Ze sloot alles d'r voor af.","lang":"Utrecht dialect","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ071310","role":"card","render":{"description":"One of eight sons was a werewolf. A werewolf could never eat his fill; he was always still hungry.","place":"Houtigehage","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/28045","original":"As der acht jonges wienen, dy't op elkoar folgen yn in húshâlding, dan wie ien fan dy acht in wjerwolf. Dat wie ien dy't noait sêd koe, dy't neat fan ûnpas kom.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"3-3"}],"hints":["Wait for the knocking. Count it.","An odd number.","7 times. That card."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_object","card":"c1","object":"door","n":7},"on_success":{"digit":{"value":7,"card":"c2"},"stack":["c2","c3","c4","c5"]}}]},{"id":4,"label":"Ghosts","digit":3,"drawers":[{"id":"4-1","type":"P6","difficulty":3.2927,"rank":0.8527,"note":"Each story one number. In this order.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ100109","role":"clip1","render":{"description":"A father wanted to lift his 10-year-old son across the canal. The boy suddenly said he saw something: a donkey or a piebald horse with a man on it. The father saw nothing, but the dog ran home terrified. The boy then saw the apparition run into the fields, and never dared to go to that spot again.","place":"Kootstertille","prov":"Fr.","year":1973,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/36744","original":"Krekt nei de lêste oarloch wienen ik en myn jonge by de Swâdde yn Twizelerheide. 't Wie sahwat by de froegere flapbrêge. Ik wie oan 'e iene kant fan 'e feart en ik soe myn jonge oerhelje. 't Is sa'n 30 jier lyn. Myn jonge is nou 40.\n\"Ik sjoch hjir hwat, heit\", sei Jan.\nJan koe net in stap mear gean. \"'t Is in ezel of in lyts bont hynderke. En dêr sit in man op\", sei er.\n\"Ik sjoch hjir neat\", sei 'k. 't Wie flakby, sei er. It hountsje dat by ús wie, wie sa deabinaud, dat it wie earder thús as wy, hoewol it oars noait by ús wei gong.\n\"Nou giet it it lân yn\", sei Jan. Midden yn 't lân waerd it wei. Jan wie sa bang, dat hy hat letter noait wer op dat plak west.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ109013","role":"clip2","render":{"description":"Of two men who promised each other that whichever died first would come and tell the other what the afterlife is like, one has died. One evening he appears at the other man's door. When the other asks him what it is like there, the dead man answers that it is not good. The surviving man never wants to talk about it again.","place":"De Westereen","prov":"Fr.","year":1974,"code":"SINSAG 0450","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/38352","original":"Der wie in man yn 'e Westerein, dy hie in maet, dat wie Geart. Hja gongen earlik en trou mei elkoarren om.\nHja biloofden elkoar, dat, deselde dy't der it earste fan har beiden ôf komme soe to reitsjen, dy soe oan 'e oare sizze hoe't it yn it hjirneimels wie.\nAlde Geart syn maet kom it earst to overlijden.\nOp in joun waerd der by Geart oan 'e doar kloppe.\n\"Folk! Folk!\" waerd der roppen. Geart hie in dûbelde doar, dat wie in boppedoar mei in ûnderdoar.\nDoe't Geart by de doar kaem stie dêr ien oer de ûnderdoar hinne leund en doe seach Geart dat it syn maet wie, dy't stoarn wie.\n\"Hoe is it dêr, jong?\" frege Geart.\n\"Net bêst\", sei syn maet.\nGeart woe dêr letter noait wer oer prate.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ118111","role":"clip3","render":{"description":"A group of boys sees two women on the dike, one in red and one in blue. The women disappear as suddenly as they appeared. They are ghosts.","place":"Garyp","prov":"Fr.","year":1979,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/31527","original":"Myn broer Wytse - dy't forstoarn is - en ik reizgen togearre nei Drylst nei in pear susters, skippersdochters, dêr't wy doe forkearing mei hienen. De moarns werom reizgen wy oer Dearsum. 't Wie dêr tusken twaën en trijen yn 'e nacht. Ik sei tsjin Wytse: \"Ik sjoch twa froulju op 'e dyk.\"\n\"Ik èk, krektlyk\", sei er.\nIk sei: \"Ien mei in reade en ien mei in blauwe jurk.\"\n\"Ik krektengelyk\", sei Wytse.\nIn skoftsje letter sei 'k: \"Ik sjoch neat mear.\"\n\"Ik ek net\", sei Wytse.\nSe wienen samar ynienen fuort. En dochs ha wy se beide klear sjoen. De reade wie hwat greater as de blauwe. Wytse en ik ha 't der letter noch faek oer hawn.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description"},"home":"4-1"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"WEV013402","role":"inside","render":{"description":"Women believe that roggemoeders (rye mothers, field spirits) are chasing them. A man on horseback lets them hold the horse by the mane and tail, so that they can escape.","place":"Muntendam","prov":"Gr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"F.W.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/44470","original":"n Poar vroulu binnen ook es vreselk schrokn onderweg.\nt Was al loat en mien voar gung op huus of.\nToun luipn door drei vroulu mit de appelsienekörven.\n(N.B.: In Muntendam woonden vroeger veel kooplieden; de vrouwen leurden met sinaasappels, vis en rode kool enz.).\nt Wazn Jantje Kip, Haarmke Snoef en schele Maarchie.\nInains begonnen ze haard te giern; de “rogge-mouers” zatn achter heur heer. Mien voader bleef stoan en zee: “Holt joe moar vaaste bie de moaze van t peerd; griep de steert.”\nDe vroulu greepn t peerd vaaste; de appelsienekörfkes bungelden op de rugge. Peerd klaude dr van deur en zo ontluipn ze de rogge-mouders.\n(Roggemouders moeten kleine wezens geweest zijn. …","lang":"Groningen dialect","front":"description","note":"This one I keep apart."},"home":"4-1"}],"hints":["Each story counts.","The first number is 10.","10 — 1 — 2."],"lock":{"kind":"number3","salt":"92011994ce294905","accepted_hashes":["3f7987c95736ceb0cf452c703ca814ea40d74d61c1bbc4ef65b725ba40a22dad"]},"on_success":{"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4"]},"found_card":{"card":"c3"}},{"id":"4-2","type":"P3","difficulty":1.3911,"rank":1.0757,"note":"One does not belong here. Back to its own cabinet.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ025502","role":"member","render":{"description":"In Westereinde two girls always haunt at night.","place":"Kollum","prov":"Fr.","year":1967,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/21287","original":"Yn 'e Westerein, yn in loantsje by 't spoar, roannen yn 'e nacht altyd twa famkes om. Dy spoeken dêr. Dêr doarsten de minsken nachts net lâns.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ093617","role":"member","render":{"description":"In the old days people sometimes saw witte wijven (white women).","place":"Rottevalle","prov":"Fr.","year":1972,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/33731","original":"Yn 'e omkriten fan Rottefalle hâldden froeger wite wiven ta.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"CJ057303","role":"intruder","render":{"description":"Several people have seen two witte wijven (white women) in the woods.","place":"Opende","prov":"Gr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25852","original":"Witte wiven gingen altyd door 't bos van Jild Dyk. En so ferdwenen se weer. 't Waren twee witte frouljuu.\nDit gebeurde faak. Forskeidene hebben se sien.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"cab:2"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"CJ057209","role":"member","render":{"description":"People used to often see a girl in black silk clothes haunting.","place":"Kollumersweach","prov":"Fr.","year":1969,"code":null,"initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/25831","original":"Op 'e Mûzewei (= Mûntse-wei) fan Aldwâld nei Feankleaster spoeke in juffer yn 't swart. Dy roan dêr altyd om. Underskate lju ha har dêr sjoen. Hja hie swart-sidene mofkes oan 'e hannen en in swart-sidene jurk hie se oan. Hja gong dêr nei in plaets ta. Dêr stie in plakje mei woartels flak by. Dêr roan se altyd oan ta, dan gong se werom. Guon seinen. hja gong ek wol nei 't slot ta. De minsken hearden de side ritseljen.","lang":"Frisian (Woudfries)","front":"description","uncatalogued":true},"home":"4-2"}],"hints":["Three cards tell essentially the same thing. The fourth does not.","The fourth is about a white woman.","The card about Opende belongs with the White Women."],"lock":{"kind":"card_to_cabinet","card":"c3","cabinet":2},"on_success":{"trail_note":2,"unlock_cabinet":2,"stack":["c1","c2","c4"]}},{"id":"4-3","type":"R4","difficulty":1.1867,"rank":0.6667,"note":"When the machine starts: let it type to the end. The rest is in here.","cards":[{"id":"c1","story_id":"CJ011305","role":"top","render":{"description":"Once when a man was out in the field, a very small brown dog floated past him. It headed for the canal.","place":"Boornbergum","prov":"Fr.","year":1966,"code":"SINSAG 0478","initials":"A.A.J.","url":"https://www.verhalenbank.nl/items/show/17744","half":"top"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c2","story_id":"CJ011305","role":"bottom","render":{"description":"The man asked what the dog wanted, but the little creature disappeared into the water. Exactly three weeks later the same thing happened to the man's father. Then too the dog seemed to disappear into the canal. The place was uncanny.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478","stain":"three"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c3","story_id":"INZ00039","role":"half","render":{"description":"But the mocking voice of the mountain spirit is heard saying that the treasure can no longer be found. A girl promises to marry, and if the marriage does not happen, to give a barrel of oil for the sanctuary lamp in the church. She marries someone else anyway, forgets her promise and dies. Her restless soul returns, but a clergyman manages to banish the ghost. Her plaintive voice is still heard: they could have helped me, but they would not.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0410"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c4","story_id":"KEUNING007203","role":"half","render":{"description":"When approached, the figure grows smaller and smaller, and when it is struck at, it is gone.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c5","story_id":"CJ060007","role":"half","render":{"description":"One day he goes to see her, and between the churchyard and the state school he sees her sitting on the right side of the path wrapped in a black cloth. He becomes frightened and returns home. Later it turns out that Griet was never there that day.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0478"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c6","story_id":"KEMP328","role":"half","render":{"description":"The parish priest finds out and one night helps the ghost priest finish the mass. The priest thanks him: during his life he had been negligent at mass, so after his death he could find no rest, but now he is released. The priest prays so fervently for the parish priest's salvation that the latter dies after only half a year.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0402"},"home":"4-3"},{"id":"c7","story_id":"CJ060905","role":"half","render":{"description":"When Schopper, the director of the Wilhelminahoeve, hears this he does not believe it, but he has to admit she is right when they see it themselves too.","half":"bottom","code":"SINSAG 0477"},"home":"4-3"}],"hints":["Read what the machine has typed, to the last word.","The rest mentions ‘dog’ again.","The number is SINSAG 0478. There are only three in the envelope."],"lock":{"kind":"card_match","top_card":"c1","bottom_card":"c2","object":"typewriter"},"on_success":{"fuse":["c1","c2"],"type_line":"Told by: the previous assistant.","digit":{"value":3,"card":"c1","word":"three","stained":"c2"},"stack":["c1","c2","c3","c4","c5","c6","c7"]}}]},{"id":5,"label":"The Devil","digit":null,"drawers":[]}]});
